---
import BaseLayout from "../site/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { siteDetails } from "../site/data/site";
import { ogImages } from "../site/data/og-images";
import "../site/styles/privacy.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy notice — Mourne Made"
  description="How Mourne Made collects, uses, stores and protects personal information submitted through this website."
  ogImage={ogImages.studio}
  ogImageAlt="Mourne Made privacy notice"
>
  <article class="privacy-page shell">
    <header class="privacy-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy notice</p>
      <h1>What happens to your information.</h1>
      <p class="lede">This notice explains the small amount of personal information Mourne Made uses when you contact the studio or visit this website.</p>
      <p class="privacy-updated">Last updated: 23 July 2026</p>
    </header>

    <div class="privacy-content">
      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-who">
        <h2 id="privacy-who">Who is responsible</h2>
        <p>{siteDetails.name} is operated by {siteDetails.founder} in {siteDetails.location}. For a privacy question or request, email <a href={siteDetails.emailHref}>{siteDetails.email}</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-collect">
        <h2 id="privacy-collect">Information collected</h2>
        <p>If you use the request form or email directly, the studio receives the details you provide: your name, email address, business or organisation, town, any public link you add, and your message. You do not have to provide a website link. Please do not send sensitive personal information through the form.</p>
        <p>Vercel hosts the website and provides cookie-free Web Analytics. The analytics integration records page views and non-identifying events such as using a comparison or starting and submitting the request form. Mourne Made does not use analytics to build personal profiles or make automated decisions.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-use">
        <h2 id="privacy-use">Why it is used</h2>
        <p>Contact details and messages are used to reply, prepare the free before-and-after you requested, discuss possible work, and keep a record of that conversation. The lawful basis is legitimate interests: responding to a request you chose to make and running the studio responsibly. The information is not used for unrelated marketing and is not sold.</p>
        <p>Aggregate website measurements are used to understand which public pages and interactions are useful, so the site and request path can be improved.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-sharing">
        <h2 id="privacy-sharing">Who processes it</h2>
        <p>Request emails are handled through Google Gmail. The website and its analytics are provided by Vercel. These providers process information on Mourne Made’s behalf under their own security and data-transfer arrangements. Information is shared with another person or organisation only when needed to provide work you request, comply with the law, or protect legal rights.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-retention">
        <h2 id="privacy-retention">How long it is kept</h2>
        <p>Enquiry emails and related project notes are kept for up to 12 months after the last contact, then deleted unless the conversation becomes paid work or a longer period is required for tax, accounting, dispute or legal records. Unsuccessful spam and abuse attempts may be retained briefly to protect the form.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-rights">
        <h2 id="privacy-rights">Your choices and rights</h2>
        <p>You can ask for a copy of your personal information, ask for inaccurate information to be corrected, ask for deletion or restriction where the law allows it, or object to processing based on legitimate interests. Email <a href={siteDetails.emailHref}>{siteDetails.email}</a> to make a request.</p>
        <p>If a privacy concern is not resolved, you can complain to the <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" rel="external">Information Commissioner’s Office (ICO)</a>, the UK data protection regulator.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-changes">
        <h2 id="privacy-changes">Changes to this notice</h2>
        <p>This page will be updated when the form, analytics, providers or uses of personal information change. The date at the top shows the current version.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
